@lang en

-- us-ch2-forms-of-acts.l4 : Title 1, chapter 2, sections 101 to 107, 106a, 106b and 114 (form and enactment of Acts).
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text); quotation lines copy it.
--
-- Encoded: the prescribed forms of words (101, 102, 105), the rules a drafted Act can be checked against (103, 104),
-- the six-day exception to the engrossing and enrolling procedure (106), and the seal (114).
-- Inert, with reasons in NOTES.md: 106 (the procedure itself), 107 (paper), and the duty to receive and publish in 106a
-- and 106b, whose day cannot be computed because "forthwith" is nowhere defined (refusals below).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-nouns`
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`

§ `Chapter 2 - Acts and Resolutions; Formalities of Enactment`

§§ `Sections 101 and 102 - the enacting clause and the resolving clause`

-- The text prints each form between quotation marks and puts the closing full stop INSIDE them. It does not say
-- whether the full stop belongs to the prescribed words, so a clause is accepted with or without it (fork F-101).
-- src:66 | The enacting clause of all Acts of Congress shall be in the following form: “Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled.”
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 101 (src:66)
GIVEN clause IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enacting clause is in the form section 101 prescribes` clause MEANS
       clause EQUALS "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
    OR clause EQUALS "Be it enacted by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled."

-- src:70 | The resolving clause of all joint resolutions shall be in the following form: “Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled.”
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 102 (src:70)
GIVEN clause IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the resolving clause is in the form section 102 prescribes` clause MEANS
       clause EQUALS "Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled"
    OR clause EQUALS "Resolved by the Senate and House of Representatives of the United States of America in Congress assembled."

§§ `Section 103 - Enacting or resolving words after the first section`

-- src:74 | No enacting or resolving words shall be used in any section of an Act or resolution of Congress except in the first.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 103 (src:74)
GIVEN section IS A `A section of an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section uses no enacting or resolving words` section MEANS
    NOT section's `it uses enacting or resolving words`

-- The first section of the list may use them and need not. Every later section must not.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 103 (src:74)
GIVEN sections IS A LIST OF `A section of an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the sections of an Act or resolution satisfy section 103` sections MEANS
    CONSIDER sections
    WHEN EMPTY                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN all `a section uses no enacting or resolving words` rest

§§ `Section 104 - Numbering of sections; single proposition`

-- "shall contain, as nearly as may be, a single proposition of enactment" is a standard of judgment, so it is inert.
-- Only the numbering is a fact a witness can read off the page.
-- src:78 | Each section shall be numbered, and shall contain, as nearly as may be, a single proposition of enactment.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 104, "Each section shall be numbered" (src:78)
GIVEN section IS A `A section of an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section is numbered` section MEANS
    section's `it carries a number`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 104, "Each section shall be numbered" (src:78)
GIVEN sections IS A LIST OF `A section of an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every section of an Act or resolution is numbered` sections MEANS
    all `a section is numbered` sections

§§ `Section 105 - Title of appropriation Acts`

-- Same punctuation fork as sections 101 and 102: the full stop sits inside the quotation marks (F-101).
-- src:82 | The style and title of all Acts making appropriations for the support of Government shall be as follows: “An Act making appropriations (here insert the object) for the year ending September 30 (here insert the calendar year).”
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 105 (src:82)
GIVEN title IS A STRING
      object IS A STRING
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the title is the title section 105 prescribes for an appropriation Act` title object year MEANS
       title EQUALS CONCAT "An Act making appropriations ", object, " for the year ending September 30 ", TOSTRING year
    OR title EQUALS CONCAT "An Act making appropriations ", object, " for the year ending September 30 ", TOSTRING year, "."

§§ `Section 106 - Printing bills and joint resolutions`

-- INERT: the procedure of engrossing, signing, sending, enrolling and presenting. It is a sequence of acts of the two Houses
-- and the President, and no fact a downstream encoding would ask about turns on it.
-- ENCODED: the last sentence, an exception that depends on a period at the end of a session.
-- src:86 | During the last six days of a session such engrossing and enrolling of bills and joint resolutions may be done otherwise than as above prescribed, upon the order of Congress by concurrent resolution.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 106, last sentence (src:86)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the session` IS A DATE
      `ordered by concurrent resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 106 permits engrossing and enrolling otherwise than as prescribed` `the date` `the last day of the session` `ordered by concurrent resolution` MEANS
        `a date falls in the last six days of a session` `the date` `the last day of the session`
    AND `ordered by concurrent resolution`

§§ `Sections 106a and 106b - Promulgation of laws; amendments to the Constitution`

-- Both sections say "forthwith": the Archivist "shall forthwith" receive a law (106a) or "shall forthwith" cause an amendment
-- to be published (106b). Title 1 defines no time word, so no day can be computed. Section 106a also names the event
-- "becomes a law or takes effect" without saying when that is; the commencement question is answered in
-- us-interpretation-time.l4.
@ref 1 U.S.C. ss 106a and 106b: "forthwith" is used and never defined
GIVETH A DATE
`Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed` MEANS
    REFUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed"

-- src:90 | Whenever a bill, order, resolution, or vote of the Senate and House of Representatives, having been approved by the President, or not having been returned by him with his objections, becomes a law or takes effect, it shall forthwith be received by the Archivist of the United States from the President
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 106a (src:90)
GIVEN `the day the bill, order, resolution or vote becomes a law or takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day by which the Archivist must receive the law from the President` `the day the bill, order, resolution or vote becomes a law or takes effect` MEANS
    `Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed`

-- src:94 | Whenever official notice is received at the National Archives and Records Administration that any amendment proposed to the Constitution of the United States has been adopted, according to the provisions of the Constitution, the Archivist of the United States shall forthwith cause the amendment to be published
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 106b (src:94)
GIVEN `the day official notice is received at the National Archives and Records Administration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day by which the Archivist must cause the amendment to be published` `the day official notice is received at the National Archives and Records Administration` MEANS
    `Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith, so the day by which the Archivist must act cannot be computed`

§§ `Section 107 - Parchment or paper for printing enrolled bills or resolutions`

-- INERT: "parchment or paper of suitable quality as shall be determined by the Joint Committee on Printing". The quality is
-- left to a body that has not been asked in this text.

§§ `Section 114 - Sealing of instruments`

-- src:205 | In all cases where a seal is necessary by law to any commission, process, or other instrument provided for by the laws of Congress, it shall be lawful to affix the proper seal by making an impression therewith directly on the paper to which such seal is necessary; which shall be as valid as if made on wax or other adhesive substance.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 114 (src:205)
GIVEN `a seal is necessary by law to the commission, process or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seal is made by an impression directly on the paper to which it is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 114 makes a seal by impression on the paper as valid as a seal on wax or other adhesive substance` `a seal is necessary by law to the commission, process or other instrument` `the seal is made by an impression directly on the paper to which it is necessary` MEANS
        `a seal is necessary by law to the commission, process or other instrument`
    AND `the seal is made by an impression directly on the paper to which it is necessary`
